r was used anywhere in the codebase or by known extensions, this is a source-incompatible change that should be documented or deprecated first."}, {"file": "services/src/main/java/org/keycloak/protocol/oidc/encode/DefaultTokenContextEncoderProviderFactory.java", "line": 82, "severity": "low", "category": "bug", "title": "Duplicate shortcut validation does not detect all collision scenarios", "body": "The check `grantsByShortcuts.size() != grantsToShortcuts.size()` only detects collisions when two grants share the same shortcut (shrinking grantsByShortcuts) or two shortcuts map to the same grant name (shrinking grantsToShortcuts). If two grants have the same shortcut AND the same ID (unlikely but possible with misconfiguration), both maps would have the same size and the collision would go undetected. A more robust approach would be to check that the number of entries inserted equals the number of grant factories iterated."}]}
